HHIISSTTOORRYY
       ppaammssccaallee  was new in Netpbm 10.20 (January 2004).  It was adapted from,
       and obsoleted, ppnnmmssccaallee.  ppaammssccaallee's primary difference  from  ppnnmmssccaallee
       is  that it handles the PAM format and uses the "pam" facilities of the
       Netpbm programming library.  But it also added the resampling class  of
       scaling  method.  Furthermore, it properly does its pixel mixing arith‐
       metic (by default) using intensity-proportional values instead  of  the
       gamma-adjusted  values  the  ppnnmmssccaallee  uses.   To  get the old ppnnmmssccaallee
       arithmetic, you can specify the --lliinneeaarr option.

       The intensity proportional stuff came out  of  suggestions  by  _A_d_a_m  _M
       _C_o_s_t_e_l_l_o in January 2004.

       The  resampling  algorithms  are  mostly taken from code contributed by
       _M_i_c_h_a_e_l _R_e_i_n_e_l_t in December 2003.

       The version of ppnnmmssccaallee from which ppaammssccaallee was derived, itself evolved
       out of the original Pbmplus version of ppnnmmssccaallee by Jef Poskanzer (1989,
       1991).  But none of that original code remains.

